    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0463" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851T.00/53: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Dakar (Flexer) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dakar</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-23">November 23,
                        1942</date>.<lb/>[Received November 26—10:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>478. Reference 477.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d455-f1"/> Conducted 11:30 to High
                    Commissioner who informed that French West Africa placed under orders Admiral
                    Darlan. Announcement made by radio Dakar 12:15. Text will follow.</p>
                <p>Incommunicado against consular staff raised and seals have been removed but High
                    Commissioner respectfully informed that reopening office in anomalous situation
                    must await Department’s instructions.</p>
                <p>Only communication from Department since reported in 477 was undecipherable
                    November 7, 6 p.m., filed 7th, received 22d.<anchor n="80" xml:id="d455-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Flexer</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d455-f1" n="79" xml:id="d455-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 477, November 14, from the Consul at Dakar, <ref target="#pg439">p.
                        439</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d455-f2" n="80" xml:id="d455-f2-content">
                <p>Circular telegram; it read: “Report to Department by quickest method local
                    reactions to current developments in Africa.” (740.0011 European War
                    1939/25303a)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
